From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Sun Jun  1 15:08:57 2003
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Sun, 01 Jun 2003 16:08:57 +0100
Subject: Re: mixed effects convergence
In-Reply-To: <OMEDKAFEGEGGFDEHGGLBAEGPDBAA.hsu@charter.net>
References: <OMEDKAFEGEGGFDEHGGLBAEGPDBAA.hsu@charter.net>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0306011603430.20222-100000@gannet.stats>

The syntax is valid, but the algorithm is having trouble fitting the 
model.  You could try increasing that limit (see ?lmeControl) but you 
probably want to think if you have enough data to fit the model you 
suggest.

Also trace the fit with options(warn=1): this might not be happening near 
the end of the fitting, in which case it can be ignored. (I am not sure if 
that can happen with lme: it can with nlme.)

