> ====================================
> Warning messages:
>     ITERATION LIMIT REACHED WITHOUT OTHER CONVERGENCE in: ms( ~  -
>         logLik(lmeSt, lmePars), start = list(lmePars = c(coef(lmeSt))),  ....
> ===================================
>
> Is there something wrong with my syntax?  I found that if I leave out Z the
> warning goes away, but I have no
> idea why.

The random structure of the model is probably too complex given the 
available data. You might do some graphical exploration to assess 
whether you really need all the random parameters you try to fit. See 
the book by the authors of lme/nlme for details:

Pinheiro, J.C. and D.M. Bates, 2000. Mixed-effect models in S and 
S-Plus. Statistics and Computing, ed. J. Chambers, et al. 2000, New 
York, Springer, 598 p.

If relevant, you might try a diagonal var-cov matrix (without cov terms) 
with:

lme(Y ~ X + Z,
    random = list(Experiment = pdDiag(form = ~ X + Z),
    data = pooled)

Best,

Renaud

