Dear S-news members,

 

I am trying to pool the results of comparative 
studies that compare two modalities of treatment. The results of each study are 
published as survival curves or probabilities. The studies vary in length of 
follow-up 5 to 14 years. I created a groupedData frame with y=survival 
probabilities, var=variance of each y, time=years (integer 1 to 14), 
 trial=factor with a level for each trial, treatment=factor with two 
levels. there are trialXtreatment groups. 

 

I am trying to use mixed models lme() and nlme() to 
pool the results and estimate the significant and magnitude of the treatment 
effect based on all studies. 

 

I used lme successfully as below however, the model 
dose not behave well at the periphery of time (predicted survival goes up at the 
left end of the predicted curve because time is modeled 
time+time^2)

 

m1.lme<-lme(y~treatment*(time+time^2)|trial/treat,data="" 
random=~time+time^2,correlation=corSpher())

 

My questions are:

 

1) How can I weight 
the survival probabilities by the inverse of their variances using the 
weights== option in lme() or nlme() ? 

 

2) For nlme: there is no self 
starting model for log-logistic or log-normal models in the nlme library with 
S-plus 6.1. Are there user contributed models? if not how can I create 
these two models?

 

 

