From spencer.graves at PDF.COM  Tue Jun  3 00:02:28 2003
From: spencer.graves at PDF.COM (Spencer Graves)
Date: Mon, 02 Jun 2003 17:02:28 -0700
Subject: Re: Matrix Power
References: <200306022353.h52NrbCu019072@fisher.utstat.toronto.edu>
Message-ID: <3EDBE594.70102@pdf.com>

You can write one easily enough:  Take the eigenvalue decomposition 
("eigen"), exponential the eigenvalues, then put the matrix back 
together.  By the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, this should work for any 
analytic function.

hope this helps.  spencer graves

