My group currently has an opening for a postdoctoral researcher 
interested in pursuing statistical algorithm development in the field 
of cancer research, neurogenomics, microarray analysis, linkage and 
haplotyping, and quantitative genetics.  The Translational Genomics 
Research Institute investigates genetic sources of disease through 
systematic genetic analysis of tissue samples, unique human populations 
specific to geographic regions throughout the world, clinical trials, 
and development of pharmacalogical lead compounds that derive directly 
from genetic studies.  TGen provides an opportunity for statistical 
growth, interaction with the world's leading cancer biologists, and 
direct access to the statistics and computer science departments at ASU 
(Tempe), NAU (Flagstaff) and U of A (Tucson).  TGen has also entered 
into an agreement with IBM life sciences to provided a top-25-ranked 
multi-CPU cluster (1024 power-4 nodes) that comes on-line in the next 
month so significant opportunities exist in the field of distributed 
statistics and supercomputing applications.  Users should be familiar 
with S+, I-miner, MatLab and/or Java with some experience with SQL.

