Date: Tue, 10 Jun 2003 08:59:10 -0400
Subject: Re: Multinomial question revisited
In-Reply-To: <001c01c32f1c$b8a0c6c0$2032b583@qut.edu.au>
References: <001c01c32f1c$b8a0c6c0$2032b583@qut.edu.au>
Message-ID: <Pine.SOL.4.10.10306100845270.28493-100000@stat.rutgers.edu>

Steve,

I am using the same example with 
    p=rep(.25,4), n=3, K=4, size=2
  
Let (X1,X1) be the two numbers randomly picked from (1,2,3,4)
  N1=min(X1,X2) and N2=max(X1,X2)

Then first row of A has a 1 in the location N1. (other elements are aeros)  
     first row of B has a 1 in the location N2. (other elements are aeros)

Joint distribution of (N1,N2) is
                    0   if n1>n2
 P(N1=n1,N2=n2)=   1/16 if n1=n2
                   2/16 if n1<n2

Conditional distribution of N2 given N1 is
 P(N2=n2 |N1=n1) = 1/16 / P(N1=n1)  if n1=n2
                   2/16 / P(N1=n1)  if n1<n2
                   0                if n1>n2

Exact calculation reveals

 P(N2 |1) ~ MN(1,p=(1 2 2 2)/7)  where N2=1,2,3,4
 P(N2 |2) ~ MN(1,p=(1,2,2)/5) where N2=2,3,4
 P(N2 |3) ~ MN(1,p=(1,2)/3) where N2=3,4
 P(N2 |4) ~ MN(1,1) where N2=4

good luck,
Jingshan

