Hi Danni,

Sounds like you're trying to create time series plots from basic
high/low level plot routines like "plot" and "lines".  S+6 and above has
a number of really good functions to handle the new "timeSeries" class
(and a lot more functionality in the FinMetrics module).  Functions such
as "plot.timeSeries" will create good quality time series plots with
lots of options.  Look at the plot.timeSeries help for more info.
You'll also need to turn your data into a timeSeries object, so have a
look at the "timeSeries" help page too ....

> myTs <- timeSeries(data.frame(matrix(rt(1000, 4), ncol=10)), 
  timeDate(julian=11001:11100))
> plot(myTs)

