From Nikhil.S.Padhye at uth.tmc.edu  Wed Jun 11 19:03:49 2003
From: Nikhil.S.Padhye at uth.tmc.edu (Nikhil S Padhye)
Date: Wed, 11 Jun 2003 14:03:49 -0500
Subject: Re: Using nonlinear least square regression
In-Reply-To: <CC189F10F7F6F744B96880AC96CBFA0E20215D@edc.gsph.pitt.edu>
Message-ID: <F567BEA12C734C4FA3DC39691BB7386914240E@UTHEVS3.mail.uthouston.edu>

Kelly,

 

In 
your formula supplied in the end to the NLS function, there is no dependence on 
Delta. You will need to ensure that this dependence is made explicit by 
defining Lamda's (and A) as functions of Delta. Otherwise, the NLS function will 
treat your secondary definitions (lamdas and A) as being fixed quantities, and 
will be unable to detect any parameter to vary.

 

Best Regards,

 

Nikhil

 

