Did you get as far as the help page for apply?  Its first argument is
an *array*, and you supplied a data frame,and did not understand 
that it would be coerced to a character matrix (and there are no NAs in 
character matrices in S-PLUS).

Use sapply on columns of a data frame, not apply(foo, 2).  In this 
case is.na(data) will give you a matrix to work with, which may be easier.

